  "changes_data": [
    {
      "diff": "@@ -3,7 +3,7 @@ include::attributes.adoc[]\n :linkcss:\n :copycss: {stylesheet}\n \n-= Wireshark {wireshark-version} Release Notes\n+== Wireshark {wireshark-version} Release Notes\n // Asciidoctor Syntax Quick Reference:\n // https://asciidoctor.org/docs/asciidoc-syntax-quick-reference/\n \n@@ -46,6 +46,22 @@ The following bugs have been fixed:\n //* cveidlink:2014-2486[]\n //* Wireshark keeps banging out random chords on your piano and yelling “LIPS LIKE SUGUAR, SUGAR KISSES” because it was funny that one time at a party.\n \n+* Fuzz job crash output: fuzz-2022-01-19-7399.pcap wsbuglink:17894[].\n+\n+* Ja3 reported is incorrect wsbuglink:17942[].\n+\n+* \"Wiki Protocol page\" in packet details menu is broken - wiki pages not migrated to GitLab? wsbuglink:17944[].\n+\n+* Dissector bug, protocol PFCP display Flow Description IE value error in Additional Flow Description of PFD Management Request Message wsbuglink:17951[].\n+\n+* Bluetooth: Fails to open Log file for SCO connection wsbuglink:17964[].\n+\n+* Fuzz job crash output: fuzz-2022-03-07-10896.pcap wsbuglink:17984[].\n+\n+* libwiretap: Save as  ERF causes segmentation fault wsbuglink:17989[].\n+\n+* HTTP server returning multiple early hints shows too many responses in \"Follow HTTP Stream\" wsbuglink:18006[].\n+\n === New and Updated Features\n \n \n@@ -63,15 +79,26 @@ There are no new protocols in this release.\n // ag -A1 '(define PSNAME|proto_register_protocol[^_])' $(git diff --name-only v3.4.9.. | ag packet- | sort -u)\n [commaize]\n --\n+IEEE 802.11\n+CSN.1\n+HTTP\n+NTLM SSP\n+PFCP\n+PKTLOG\n+SSDP\n+TLS\n+USB HID\n --\n \n === New and Updated Capture File Support\n \n-There is no new or updated capture file support in this release.\n+// There is no new or updated capture file support in this release.\n // Add one file type per line between the -- delimiters.\n-// [commaize]\n-// --\n-// --\n+[commaize]\n+--\n+pcap\n+pcapng\n+--\n \n === New File Format Decoding Support\n \n",
